  {
   "id": 38,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1900,
    -680
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 37,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "INSANE IMAGE-TO-IMAGE \u2014 Flux.1-dev fp8\n\nPIPELINE\ninput \u2192 (depth + canny [+ pose]) via ControlNet Union Pro 2.0\n\u2192 PuLID identity \u2192 img2img KSampler \u2192 FaceDetailer \u2192\n4\u00d7-UltraSharp + 2\u00d7 tiled refine. Saves at every stage:\n01_base / 02_face_detailed / 03_final_upscaled.\n\nQUICK START\n1) Upload input_image.png (composition source) and\n   face_reference.png (clean frontal face of YOUR character).\n2) Positive prompt: describe the RESULT you want, not the input.\n3) The single most important dial \u2014 KSampler DENOISE:\n   0.25\u20130.35  keep structure, change surface (relight/retexture)\n   0.40\u20130.55  balanced re-render (default 0.50)\n   0.60\u20130.75  heavy reimagining; ControlNets hold pose/layout\n4) Queue. Full pipeline \u2248 2\u20133 min on A100 80GB @1.5 MP + 2\u00d7.\n\nNo face reference yet? Bypass (Ctrl+B) the ApplyPulidFlux node \u2014\neverything else runs identically."
   ],
   "title": "\u2460 READ ME \u2014 INSANE IMAGE-TO-IMAGE",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1340,
    -680
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 38,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "REQUIRED FILES \u2014 download_models.sh fetches everything.\n\ndiffusion_models/flux1-dev-fp8-e4m3fn.safetensors\ntext_encoders/clip_l.safetensors\ntext_encoders/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors\nvae/ae.safetensors\ncontrolnet/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0.safetensors\npulid/pulid_flux_v0.9.1.safetensors\ninsightface/models/antelopev2/   (5 onnx files)\nultralytics/bbox/face_yolov8m.pt\nsams/sam_vit_b_01ec64.pth\nupscale_models/4x-UltraSharp.pth\nclip_vision/sigclip_vision_patch14_384.safetensors  (Redux)\nstyle_models/flux1-redux-dev.safetensors  (optional \u00b7 gated \u00b7\n  set WITH_REDUX=true + HF_TOKEN)\n\nEVA-CLIP (PuLID) + DepthAnythingV2 + DWPose weights auto-download\non the first queue \u2014 first run is slower than normal."
   ],
   "title": "\u2461 MODELS",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -780,
    -680
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 39,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "CONTROLNET \u2014 Union Pro 2.0. One model, all modes (canny, soft\nedge, depth, pose, gray). v2.0 removed the mode embedding, so\nNO type-selector node is needed \u2014 the mode is implied by the\ncontrol image you feed each Apply stage.\n\nACTIVE:   DEPTH 0.60/end 0.60 \u00b7 CANNY 0.45/end 0.50\nBYPASSED: POSE stage \u2014 Ctrl+B it ON for people shots where the\n          pose must lock exactly (then consider canny \u2192 0.35).\n\nstrength    = how hard it steers\nend_percent = when it lets go. Releasing control at 0.5\u20130.7\nlets Flux invent clean detail in the final steps \u2014 leaving\ncontrol at 1.0 is the #1 cause of crunchy artifacts.\n\nHigh denoise (>0.6) \u2192 raise strengths ~+0.10.\nStructure-only restyle: depth 0.70/end 0.80, canny bypassed.\nLine-art faithful:      canny 0.60/end 0.70, depth 0.40."
   ],
   "title": "\u2462 CONTROL",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -220,
    -680
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 40,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "PuLID-Flux + optional character LoRA.\n\nPuLID weight: 0.70\u20130.80 subtle \u00b7 0.85 default \u00b7 0.95\u20131.05 max\nlock (too high = pasted-on face that fights relighting).\nstart_at 0.0 / end_at 1.0 default; raise start_at to 0.1\u20130.2 if\nidentity overrides composition too early.\n\nface_reference: sharp, frontal-ish, evenly lit, ONE face,\nface \u2265 512 px. Renders from this same workflow are ideal.\n\nSTRONGEST STACK: character LoRA (un-bypass the LoRA node,\n0.7\u20130.9) for body/hair/overall identity + PuLID at 0.6\u20130.8 for\nthe face lock. Train the LoRA on stills this workflow produces.\n\nNOTE: your PuLID node pack may expose extra widgets (fusion\nmethod etc.) \u2014 defaults are correct; only weight/start/end\nmatter day-to-day.\n\nIdentity tools are for YOUR original character (or people who\nexplicitly consented) \u2014 never for replicating real people."
   ],
   "title": "\u2463 IDENTITY",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    340,
    -680
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 41,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "SAMPLER: 28 steps \u00b7 euler/beta \u00b7 FluxGuidance 3.5.\nGuidance 2.5\u20133.0 = softer, more photographic;\n4.0\u20134.5 = stricter prompt adherence, more contrast.\nFlux uses guidance, NOT cfg \u2014 keep KSampler cfg at 1.0 ALWAYS.\n\nFACEDETAILER: auto-detects the face, re-renders it at 1024 px\nwith the SAME identity stack. denoise 0.45 default\n(0.30 gentle fix \u00b7 0.55 full rebuild).\n\nULTIMATE UPSCALE: 4\u00d7-UltraSharp model pass, then 2\u00d7 tiled\nrefine at denoise 0.22 (0.15 safest \u00b7 0.30 adds texture but can\ndrift), 1024 px tiles. Final \u2248 6 MP / ~3000 px wide.\n\nINPUT SIZE: 1.5 MP working resolution (Flux sweet spot 1\u20132 MP).\n\nWORKFLOW RHYTHM: seed \u2192 randomize, queue 4\u20138, pick the winner,\nfix that seed, then tune denoise/weights around it."
   ],
   "title": "\u2464 QUALITY LADDER",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    900,
    -680
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 42,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "REDUX = style/vibe transfer from a reference image, applied to\nthe positive conditioning before the ControlNets.\n\nENABLE: un-bypass the REDUX apply node (Ctrl+B) and load\nstyle_reference.png. Requires the gated flux1-redux-dev model\n(WITH_REDUX=true + HF_TOKEN in the pod env).\n\nstrength 0.3\u20130.5 = subtle palette/lighting/mood transfer\nstrength 0.6\u20130.8 = strong look transfer (starts to override\nyour text prompt).\n\nKILLER USE-CASE: lock one hero image's grade + lighting across\nan entire content set \u2014 same character, same look, dozens of\nposes/scenes."
   ],
   "title": "\u2465 REDUX STYLE (bypassed)",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
